@startuml
title Approved Expense and Payment Balance Effects (Both scopes; proposed)
left to right direction

rectangle "Approved Expense\namount A" as Expense
rectangle "Payer credit\n+A" as Credit
rectangle "Participant debit\n-share" as Debit
rectangle "Exact ledger entries\nsum to zero" as Ledger
rectangle "Group + currency net positions" as Net
rectangle "Deterministic debtor/creditor\nmatching policy (approval needed)" as Match
rectangle "Outstanding balance\nD owes C" as Due
rectangle "Payment P from D to C\n0 < P <= due" as Payment
rectangle "Updated balance\ndue - P" as Updated
rectangle "Reject excess payment;\nshow amount due" as Reject

Expense --> Credit
Expense --> Debit
Credit --> Ledger
Debit --> Ledger
Ledger --> Net
Net --> Match
Match --> Due
Due --> Payment
Payment --> Updated
Due --> Reject : P > due

note bottom
  Payer may be a participant; their credit and own share debit offset.
  Payment records settlement and does not initiate a money transfer.
  Netting algorithm across multiple debtors/creditors is not defined by the spec.
end note
@enduml
